The trust policy defines who is allowed to assume the role, while the permissions policy defines what the role can do after it is assumed. 

If the trust policy allows lambda.amazonaws.com instead of ec2.amazonaws.com, 
an EC2 instance cannot assume or use the role, even if the role has S3 permissions.






